The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (S.len > 1) {
    if      (dir == LEFT  && S.dir == RIGHT)
        S.dir = RIGHT;
    else if (dir == RIGHT && S.dir == LEFT)
        S.dir = LEFT;
    else if (dir == UP    && S.dir == DOWN)
        S.dir = DOWN;
    else if (dir == DOWN  && S.dir == UP)
        S.dir = UP;
}
```
Reason:
The condition `if (S.len > 1)` restricts the snake from changing direction when its length is greater than 1. This prevents valid direction changes that should be allowed, leading to incorrect behavior in the game as the snake cannot navigate properly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
else
    S.dir = dir;
```
Reason:
The addition of `else S.dir = dir;` allows the snake to change its direction regardless of its length, enabling valid direction changes and restoring proper navigation behavior in the game.

